Hey Rajan, wiping his tear-filled eyes and his breasts soaked with the tears of sorrow,
Lord, the goal of his devotees, embraced his virtuous wife, who was the only one
wanting him. Shri Krishna, skilled in the art of giving solace, gently encouraged the pathetic Rukmini.
He bound her, whose mind was deluded by the clever laughter and jokes of God, and who was not worthy of suffering in this way.
